    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customer-code de-duplication in `OwnerRestControllerV1.generateCustomerCode` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`).\n\nThe `customerCode` was previously a pure function of `<REGION>-<HASH8>` \u2014 meaning two distinct owners whose `(telephone, lastName)` pair hashes to the same value (and share a region) would receive identical codes. I:\n\n1. Extracted the computed value into a `base`, then routed it through a new `deduplicateCustomerCode(base)` helper.\n2. The helper collects all existing owners' non-null `customerCode`s into a set. If `base` is unused, it's returned unchanged. Otherwise it appends `-<n>`, starting at `n = 2` and incrementing to the smallest value that produces a code no existing owner carries (e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-2`, then `-3`, \u2026).\n\nThis preserves the existing derived-value behavior: `getLocality()` still reads the region segment via the *first* `-`, so a de-duplicated suffix doesn't disturb it, and the membership number continues to build off the (now unique) customer code.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` acceptance test, which asserts distinct owners always receive distinct customer codes, passes).",
